    description: "Nalanda, about 90 km southeast of Patna, traces its history back to the time of the Buddha, though the university itself was founded in the 5th century CE and flourished for roughly 700 years, teaching Buddhist scripture, philosophy, theology, logic, grammar, astronomy, and medicine to scholars from across Asia. Its decline began in the late Pala period, and the final blow came with Bakhtiyar Khilji's invasion around 1200 CE. Chinese travellers Hiuen-Tsang and I-Tsing left detailed accounts of the university at its height — accounts that, along with the excavated ruins, are much of what's known about it today. A UNESCO World Heritage Site, the ruins still show lecture halls, dormitories, and stupas laid out across the sprawling campus.",
