    description: "Nahargarh Fort was built in 1734 by Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II atop the ridge overlooking Jaipur, originally named Sudarshangarh before taking on its current name — \"abode of tigers\" — from local tradition holding that the spirit of Nahar Singh Bhomia repeatedly obstructed its construction until a memorial temple to him was built within the fort walls. Its fortified walls run along the surrounding hills to connect with Jaigarh Fort above Amber, forming a single defensive network that once guarded the city. The fort was extended in 1868 under Sawai Ram Singh, and between 1883-92 gained the Madhavendra Bhawan, a striking range of palaces built by Sawai Madho Singh with matching suites for each of Jaipur's queens and a central suite for the king himself — today the fort is best known for its genuinely sweeping sunset views over the Pink City below.",
