    description: "Morni combines myth, mystery, and history in the lower reaches of the Shivalik range — Haryana's one genuine hill station, offering cool climate, natural vistas, and real opportunities for trekking and rock-climbing. Just five hours from Delhi and 45 km from Chandigarh, it sits at roughly 3,600 feet, with pines crowning the hilltops and neem, oak, pipal, jamun, amaltas, and jacaranda covering the slopes — trees originally introduced here as an experimental venture. Its two large, mysteriously interconnected lakes (tals) — separated by a hillock yet always at matching water levels — are considered auspicious by locals, who gather here for ceremonial occasions; a small temple on the bank holds a Trimurti dating back to the 12th century AD, alongside the remains of an old fort.",
