    state: "Haryana",
    tagline: "A Ramsar Wetland Right on Delhi's Doorstep",
    description: "Sultanpur National Park and Bird Sanctuary sits in Gurugram district, 46 km from Delhi and 15 km from Gurugram on the Gurugram–Farrukh Nagar Road — lush with trees, shrubs, and clusters of bougainvillea. Four watchtowers (machans) at different points make bird-watching genuinely accessible, alongside adequate parking, toilets, and drinking-water facilities; an Educational Interpretation Centre offers proper guidance for visitors. A good pair of binoculars is essential to clearly observe the wildlife from a safe distance without disturbing it — the park draws serious birders as much as casual weekend visitors, especially through the winter migratory season.",
