    name: "The Kala Amb Park",
    state: "Haryana",
    tagline: "Where the Third Battle of Panipat Was Fought",
    description: "A well-known site where the Third Battle of Panipat was fought, Kala Amb sits 8 km from Panipat city. The Marathas arrived in north India believing they could reshape Indian polity for good — but, like Ibrahim Lodhi before them, ended up antagonizing potential allies, and were ultimately surrounded by Afghan forces in a brutal clash. In one corner of the park stands a red obelisk marking the spot where Maratha commander Sadashiv Rao Bhau fell in battle. Local legend holds that a black mango tree once stood at this exact spot, under which Bhau fought his last action — the tree is long gone, but it passed its name on to the park: Kala Amb, 'black mango.'",
